<title>FINLAND: MERITA 9-MTH PROFIT RISES 93 PERCENT.</title>
<headline>MERITA 9-MTH PROFIT RISES 93 PERCENT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to end-Sept, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating profit after credit losses	 930 vs 482</p>
<p> Net loan and guarantee losses		1,144 vs 1,093</p>
<p> Net income from financial operations     3,026 vs 2,756</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		   0.98 vs 0.61</p>
<p> Capital adequacy (BIS), percent	     10.8 vs 10.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The median of analysts' forecasts for banking group</p>
<p>Merita was for a 952 million markka operating profit after</p>
<p>credit losses (range 800 million to 1,060 million).</p>
<p> Interest income				  9,750 vs 10,563</p>
<p> Net income from leasing			  243 vs 218</p>
<p> Interest expenses				6,967 vs 8,024</p>
<p> NET INCOME FROM FINANCIAL OPERATIONS     3,026 vs 2,756</p>
<p> Dividend income				    155 vs 178</p>
<p> Commission income, expenses		  1,682 vs 1,469</p>
<p> Net income from securities transactions    873 vs 399</p>
<p> Net income from forex dealings		 149 vs 203</p>
<p> Other operating income			   993 vs 713</p>
<p> TOTAL INCOME				     6,877 vs 5,719</p>
<p> Personnel expenses			     2,255 vs 2,193</p>
<p> Other expenses				   1,938 vs 1,628</p>
<p> Depreciation					 745 vs 336</p>
<p> TOTAL EXPENSES				   4,938 vs 4,157</p>
<p> NET CREDIT LOSSES				1,144 vs 1,093</p>
<p>Profit from companies</p>
<p> carried under equity method		    136 vs 25</p>
<p> PROFIT ON ORDINARY OPERATIONS		  930 vs 482</p>
<p> Extraordinary gain				 nil vs nil</p>
<p> Extraordinary expenses			    56 vs 293</p>
<p> PROFIT BEFORE APPROPRIATIONS AND TAXES     875 vs 189</p>
<p> Change in reserves			  charge 7 vs 5 gain</p>
<p> Direct taxes					 100 vs 30</p>
<p> Minorities					    15 vs 14</p>
<p> NET PROFIT					   753 vs 150</p>
<p>NOTES - Nine-month figures from 1995 do not include data for</p>
<p>Kansallis-Osake-Pankki's first quarter but Merita also stated</p>
<p>new proforma figures including KOP's first quarter. These put</p>
<p>1995 Jan-Sept operating profit after credit losses at 165</p>
<p>million markka.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
